1
00:04:09,599 --> 00:04:15,599
A story of natural love.

2
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:25,199
The Blue Lagoon is a adventure, drama, romance film directed by Randal Kleiser.

3
00:12:28,799 --> 00:12:34,799
Two small children and a ship's cook survive a shipwreck and
find safety on an idyllic tropical island.

4
00:16:38,399 --> 00:16:44,399
Soon, however, the cook dies and the young boy and girl are left on their own.

5
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Days become years and Emmeline and Richard make a home for themselves
surrounded by exotic creatures and nature's beauty.

6
00:24:57,599 --> 00:25:03,599
But will they ever see civilization again?

7
00:29:07,200 --> 00:29:13,200
Emmeline, played by Brooke Shields.

8
00:33:16,799 --> 00:33:22,799
Richard, played by Christopher Atkins.

9
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:32,400
Paddy Button, played by Leo McKern.

10
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:42,000
Arthur Lestrange, played by William Daniels.

11
00:45:45,599 --> 00:45:51,599
Lookout, played by Jeffrey Kleiser.

12
00:49:55,199 --> 00:50:01,199
Officer, played by Gus Mercurio.

13
00:54:04,799 --> 00:54:10,799
The Blue Lagoon is a 1980 American drama film directed by Randal Kleiser from a screenplay written by
Douglas Day Stewart based on the 1908 novel of the same name by Henry De Vere Stacpoole.

14
00:58:14,400 --> 00:58:20,400
The film stars Brooke Shields and Christopher Atkins.

15
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
The music score was composed by Basil Poledouris, and the
cinematography was by Néstor Almendros.

16
01:06:33,599 --> 01:06:39,599
The film tells the story of a boy and a girl who live together in a tropical
island paradise in the South Pacific after surviving a shipwreck.

17
01:10:43,199 --> 01:10:49,199
Without adult supervision or societal restrictions, the two navigate the emotional and physical changes of
puberty, fall in love, and have a child together before being rescued at the film's end.

18
01:14:52,800 --> 01:14:58,800
The Blue Lagoon was theatrically released on June 20, 1980 by Columbia Pictures.

19
01:19:02,399 --> 01:19:08,399
The film was panned by critics, who disparaged its screenplay, its execution, and
Shields' performance; however, Almendros' cinematography received praise.

20
01:23:12,000 --> 01:23:18,000
In spite of the criticism, the film was a commercial success, grossing $58.8 million on a $4.5
million budget and becoming the ninth-highest-grossing film of 1980 in North America.

21
01:27:21,599 --> 01:27:27,599
The film was nominated for the Saturn Award for Best Fantasy Film, the Academy Award for Best
Cinematography for Almendros, and the Golden Globe Award for New Star of the Year – Actor for Atkins.

22
01:31:31,199 --> 01:31:37,199
Shields won the inaugural Golden Raspberry Award for
Worst Actress for her work in the film.

23
01:35:40,800 --> 01:35:46,800
The film explores themes of sexual identity,
shipwreck, melancholy, lovers, stranded.

24
01:39:50,399 --> 01:39:56,399
The tone is emotional.
